<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends firmer in a dull session.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends firmer in a dull session.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka closed firmer at 43.7600/7800 to the dollar in a dull interbank session on Saturday against a previous close at 43.7700/8000, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said transactions had been poor mainly due to the closure of international markets.</p>
<p>Interbank call money rates closed at seven to nine percent against a previous 7.5 to 9.0, dealers said.</p>
<p>- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
